/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  heatExchanger05_bell_delaware_auto
  ==================================

  The SAME exchanger as heatExchanger04_bell_delaware_rating, with the four
  chart readings replaced by the word `auto`: JL, JB, RL and RB are COMPUTED
  by Taborek's closed forms (HEDH 3.3, as printed in Goncalves, Costa &
  Bagajewicz, AIChE J. 2019, and Mohammadi et al., arXiv:1810.02243):

      JL = 0.44(1-rs) + [1-0.44(1-rs)] exp(-2.2 rlm)
      JB = exp[-C Fsbp (1-(2 Nss/Nc)^(1/3))]        C = 1.25 (Re > 100)
      RL = exp[-1.33 (1+rs) rlm^p]                  p = 0.8 - 0.15 (1+rs)
      RB = exp[-Cbp Fsbp (1-(2 Nss/Nc)^(1/3))]      Cbp = 3.7 (Re > 100)

  with rs = Ssb/(Ssb+Stb) and rlm = (Ssb+Stb)/Sm.  The glass-box choice is
  the student's: each factor is a declared chart number or `auto`, and the
  run says which it took.  Against the book's chart readings (0.58, 0.92,
  0.33, 0.76) the forms give 0.556, 0.916, 0.327, 0.771 on this geometry:
  JL is the weakest, 4 % low, so h falls by about the same amount.  J_r and
  J_s are not applied (Hewitt applies neither); R_s is not used.

  GEOMETRY: the bundle of Hewitt's Example 6.1 (shell 0.5398 m, 158 tubes of
  25.4 mm OD on a 31.75 mm square pitch, 127 mm baffle spacing, 25 % cut,
  four tube passes).  The chart coordinates -- (Ssb+Stb)/Sm, Ssb/(Ssb+Stb),
  Fbp, Nss/Nc -- depend on the geometry alone, so the book's readings
  (0.58, 0.92, 0.33, 0.76) hold here for water: the run PUBLISHES the
  coordinates (BD_leakageRatio, BD_leakageSplit, BD_Fbp) so a student can
  check them against the charts.  The textbook example itself (a light
  hydrocarbon) is reproduced digit by digit by the props bench
  tutorials/props/heat/bellDelaware01_hewitt_example62.

  Properties are the package's, evaluated at each stream's inlet
  temperature.  The tube side is Gnielinski; the overall U and the eps-NTU
  duty are unchanged from `model geometry;`.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

// stream state lives on disk in 0/ (per-stream files); flowsheetDict is TOPOLOGY only

units
(
    {
        name        hx;
        type        heatExchanger;
        model       BellDelaware;
        inputs      ( hotShell  coldTube );
        outputs     ( hotOut  coldOut );

        operation
        {
            flow        counter;
            tubeStream  coldTube;        // which inlet is inside the tubes

            geometry
            {
                tubeID         0.020574 m;
                tubeOD         0.0254 m;
                tubeLength     4.8768 m;
                nTubes         158;
                passes         4;
                shellID        0.5398 m;
                baffleSpacing  0.1270 m;
                tubePitch      0.03175 m;
                tubePattern    square;
                wallMaterial   carbonSteel;   // -> k = 50 W/(m.K)
            }

            tubeSide  { model Gnielinski; }

            //  The shell side (Hewitt Section 6.3.2).  JL, JB, RL, RB are
            //  COMPUTED (`auto`) instead of read from Bell's charts.
            bellDelaware
            {
                baffleCutPercent     25;
                bundleShellClearance 0.035 m;
                tubeBaffleClearance  0.0008 m;
                shellBaffleClearance 0.005 m;
                sealingStripRatio    0.2;     // N_ss/N_c, chart parameter
                baffleThickness      0.005 m;
                idealBank            Hewitt;
                JL auto;  JB auto;            // Taborek closed forms
                RL auto;  RB auto;
            }
        }
    }
);
